%description:

DcTcp.g:other -- after one window of marked data, alpha is g.

The claim (DcTcp.ned): "the estimation gain g of the fraction of marked bytes, alpha (RFC 8257
section 4.2)".

The classes: rfc8257 (1/16, the default of RFC 8257 section 4.2), other (another value up to
1), invalid (0 and less, above 1). The code: DcTcp updates alpha once each window,
alpha = alpha * (1 - g) + g * F, from 0, and emits it as calcLoad (DcTcp::processEce()). This test separates "other" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp and tcpEcnMode "rfc3168" (preconditions), which sends
100000 bytes; the tap marks each data segment of host1 CE, so the fraction F is 1.
Observation: level 2, the first value of the signal calcLoad is g, 1.

%# parameter: DcTcp.g
%# class: other
%# value: 1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.g
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("DcTcpGOther")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                     .set("ipv4.ecn", "3")
                     .describe("each data segment of host1: mark it CE"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("calcLoad")
                  .first()
                  .assertValueBetween(0.999, 1.001)
                  .describe("the first alpha, after one window of marked data")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "DcTcpGOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.g = 1    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST DcTcpGOther: PASS
